WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.420
Hey everyone, welcome to Tesla's short time, Daily, Episode 489.

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:07.860
It's May 28, 2026, and I'm Patrick in Vancouver.

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.060
Tesla never sleeps and neither do's the news cycle.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:15.980
Tesla's Roadster now has a confirmed Austin Gigafactory production site,

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:17.980
yet no release date has been set.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:24.160
Executives confirm the next-generation Roadster will be built at the Texas facility alongside other models.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:29.560
The move resolves long-standing questions about where the low-volume holocar would be assembled,

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:35.440
not timeline for customer deliveries was provided, leaving the project still years from volume

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:40.920
output. The decision aligns with Tesla's pattern of consolidating high-complexity vehicles

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:44.780
at Giga, Texas rather than spreading production across multiple sites.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:49.480
From long horizon halo cars to near-term robotics ambitions,

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.240
shift to the Optimus program's current constraint.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:57.940
Tesla's timeline for scaling the Optimus robot has hit a manufacturing constraint that

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:04.020
executives have not yet detailed publicly. The snag arrives as Giga Texas prepares dedicated

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:10.240
assembly space for the project. Current plans still target initial volume production in 2027,

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:14.480
but the delay could compress the testing window before wider deployment.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:20.260
Observers will watch for updates on actuator or sensor supply chains in the coming quarters.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:26.220
While hardware timelines tighten, the autonomy side of the business is also facing real-world

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:31.640
friction. The number of vehicles operating in unsupervised or limited supervision mode in

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:37.740
Austin, Dallas and Houston has declined. The reduction follows early reports of operational

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:43.960
adjustments in those cities. Regulators continue to review data on real-world performance before

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:49.660
any broader expansion. The change highlights the gap between current supervised capability

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:56.660
and the regulatory bar for driverless service. The same reliability questions surfacing externally

00:01:56.660 --> 00:02:00.380
are also being raised internally by the people training the system.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:06.560
Internal trainers have flag discrepancies between Tesla's published safety statistics

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:10.020
and observed edge case performance during training sessions.

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:15.480
The concerns center on how rare events are captured and weighted in the data pipeline.

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:21.520
This feedback loop directly influenced the next iteration of the full self-driving software stack.

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:27.360
Regulators reviewing unsupervised deployment will likely examine these internal assessments.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:33.560
Even as autonomy questions linger, manufacturing improvements on the energy side continue to move

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:39.940
forward. Elon Musk stated that the manufacturing shift to dry cathode electrodes will meaningfully

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:45.780
lower battery pack expenses. The technique eliminates solvent recovery steps and reduces energy

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:51.420
use during production. Tesla is scaling the process at both gigatex and Nevada facilities.

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:56.980
Cost curves from this change will be tracked in upcoming earnings reports. While battery

00:02:56.980 --> 00:03:01.740
production advances, the next generation sports car remains a separate engineering challenge.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:08.660
Vehicle engineering, VPLRs, Moravie noted that adding a third motor to the Model 3 would require

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:14.480
significant chassis and thermal redesign work. The project remains secondary to roadster development.

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:20.100
Existing dual motor hardware already delivers strong performance, so the trim motor variant

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:24.880
is not a near-term priority. Any launch would likely follow roadster production ramp.

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:30.660
From vehicle engineering trade-offs to early real-world testing of the robot taxi concept itself.

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:35.860
A vehicle matching the CyberCab design was spotted on public roads in the city.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:41.380
The sighting provided the first visual confirmation of testing outside controlled environments

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:47.480
since the Wii robot unveiling. No details on sensor configuration or supervision level were

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:52.980
available from observers. Continued sightings will indicate how quickly the program is moving toward

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:59.200
wider validation. Hardware validation on the road pairs naturally with longer-term breakthroughs

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:05.620
happening in adjacent companies. The company patented a PCTFE-based method that creates

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:11.600
hermetic seals around thousands of ultra-thin polyamide ribbons. The technique avoids shattering

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:17.100
traditional materials when drilling high density feed-throughs. It also enables wireless charging

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:23.220
and data transmission through the skull without external antennas. The process is already in use

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:28.820
for the roughly 20 participants in current human trials. This manufacturing step removes

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:34.740
a key limit on electro-deck count for future higher bandwidth versions. If the same vertical

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:40.060
integration logic Tesla applies to vehicle and battery production extends to medical hardware,

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:45.660
the bottleneck on scaling channel counts disappears. Production could shift from specialized

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:50.940
clean-room craftsmanship toward automated lines capable of supporting tens of thousands of

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:56.300
electrodes per implant. That shift would change both the economics of brain computer interfaces

00:04:56.300 --> 00:05:02.380
and the timeline for broader clinical use. Keep an eye on actuator and sensor supply chain updates

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:09.920
for optimism in the coming quarters. That's your Tesla news for today. TSLA closed at $440.36

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:20.060
up $6.77 1.6%. If you found this useful, a rating or review on Apple podcasts or Spotify really

